@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Instruction injection — proveo's default instructions reach the agent without touching the project, and the project's own AGENTS.md is read
' purpose: where the def's default instructions go, and how Claude Code under sbx reads a project's AGENTS.md
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_seed_instructions, proveo_claude_reads_agents_md, _proveo_drop_block)
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/opencode/managed/opencode.json
' covers: internal/contract/instructions_seed_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/seed_phase_test.go
' covers: internal/imagetest/claudecode_test.go
' covers: internal/imagetest/opencode_test.go
' covers: e2e/scope_mounts_test.go
'   the seed and its release point ... _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
'   the house rules (user layer) ..... _spec/packages/lib/house-rules.puml
'   the clone the snapshot commits ... _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
'   the research (2026-11-11) ........ scratchpad agents-md-research.md of session e2da2921
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT WAS WRONG (2026-11-11) ────────────────────────────────────────────
' claudecode (proveo_seed_instructions) and opencode (seed_project_agents_md)
' copied the def's default AGENTS.md INTO the workspace when it carried
' neither AGENTS.md nor CLAUDE.md. Teardown's clone snapshot (`git add -A`)
' then committed it, so a run where the agent changed nothing reported
' "<branch> (1 new commit)", and the git-sync turn hook committed it too.
' The operator asked: "could the seed be directly injected as LLM context,
' without modifying the project's AGENTS.md instead?"
'
' ── THE DECISION (the operator, 2026-11-11) ────────────────────────────────
' Option A: the default goes to a VM-local tier, per boot.
'   claudecode  a marked block in the managed /etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md
'               (PROVEO_DEFAULTS_START/END), written by _proveo_write_block and
'               taken out by _proveo_drop_block when the workspace carries
'               either file, so a kept sandbox's restart follows the project
'   opencode    /dev/shm/proveo-default-instructions.md, which the image's
'               system config /etc/opencode/opencode.json lists under
'               "instructions" (a union across documents, loaded after the
'               AGENTS.md files); removed when the workspace carries either file
' The workspace is never written. Nothing persists on the host.
' NOT CHOSEN: B, `--append-system-prompt-file` and OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT at
' launch (Claude's subagents miss it; more plumbing); C, keep the file and
' hide it with .git/info/exclude (the worktree is still modified, and with
' --clone=false the exclude lands in the operator's checkout); the user
' instruction files (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, ~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md), which
' sync to ~/.proveo and would leak one project's default into every run.
' The /etc/opencode floor: @opencode/cli >= 2.0.30, asserted by the Dockerfile.
' /etc/opencode/opencode.json holds only "instructions": a managed scalar
' would override the operator's own config.
'
' ── CLAUDE CODE UNDER SBX DID NOT READ A PROJECT'S AGENTS.md ───────────────
' Claude Code reads AGENTS.md only when no CLAUDE.md exists in the cwd or
' above it (code.claude.com/docs/en/memory). sbx's agent-context@1 writes its
' environment profile as CLAUDE.md in the workspace's PARENT directory
' (sandbox-kit-spec: "the workspace directory's sibling when directory is
' omitted"; internal/sbx/third_party/claude.yaml). So every project AGENTS.md
' under sbx was hidden, the seeded default included.
' MEASURED (2026-11-11, Claude Code 2.1.312, sbx v0.50.0, one throwaway repo
' with a marker line in AGENTS.md, `claude -p` asked to repeat the marker):
'   published image ............................... NONE
'   pluginConfigs in managed-settings.d drop-in ... NONE
'   the drop-in plus an empty managed-settings.json NONE
'   pluginConfigs in managed-settings.json ........ NONE
'   the drop-in, /etc/claude-code owned by root ... NONE
'   the same JSON through --settings .............. the marker
'   the same JSON in ~/.claude/settings.json ...... the marker
' Each NONE session's transcript listed only /etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md and
' the sibling CLAUDE.md. The docs say managed settings carry pluginConfigs;
' on 2.1.312 they do not.
' THE FIX (the operator chose user settings over --settings at launch):
' proveo_claude_reads_agents_md merges
'   pluginConfigs."cc-plugin-agents-md@builtin".options.instructionFiles =
'   "claude-md-and-agents-md"
' into the sandbox's ~/.claude/settings.json on every seed, before the
' release, and leaves a value the operator already set. Every claude in the
' sandbox reads it, IDE and `sbx exec` sessions included. It persists in
' ~/.proveo/.claude/settings.json, never in the operator's own ~/.claude.
' After the fix, on the same repo: the marker. On a bare repo: a clean
' worktree, the managed block present, no /dev/shm file for claudecode.
' NOT VERIFIED LIVE: opencode (no proveo/opencode image on the host); the
' full image builds (the probes overlaid the changed files on the published
' claudecode image).
'
' Pinned by internal/contract/instructions_seed_test.go:
'   TestInstructionSeedPutsDefaultsInVMLocalContextAndNeverInTheWorkspace
'   TestTheOpencodeImageListsTheDefaultsWhereOpencodeReadsThem
'   TestTheSeedSetsClaudeCodeToLoadAgentsMdBesideClaudeMd
'   TestSeedReleasesTheAgentAfterConfigAndBeforeInstalls
' Pinned by internal/imagetest: the claudecode seed sets instructionFiles;
'   /etc/opencode/opencode.json lists the defaults file.
' Pinned by e2e: TestWorktreeWorkspaceIsFullyUsable (a clean worktree and the
'   managed block; needs a claudecode image built from this source).

component "the workspace\nthe operator's project" as WS <<data>>
component "proveo_seed_instructions\nper boot, before the release" as SEED <<app>>
component "/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md\nhouse rules + the default block" as MANAGED <<host>>
component "/dev/shm/proveo-default-instructions.md\nlisted by /etc/opencode/opencode.json" as SHM <<host>>
component "sbx's CLAUDE.md\nbeside the workspace" as SIB <<cloud>>
component "~/.claude/settings.json\ninstructionFiles: both" as SET <<data>>
component "the agent\nclaudecode · opencode" as AGENT <<app>>

SEED ARROW_MAIN MANAGED : claudecode
SEED ARROW_MAIN SHM : opencode
SEED ARROW_ERROR WS : never written
SEED ARROW_MAIN SET : claudecode
MANAGED ARROW_MAIN AGENT
SHM ARROW_MAIN AGENT
WS ARROW_MAIN AGENT : its own AGENTS.md
SIB ARROW_ERROR AGENT : hid AGENTS.md until SET

note bottom of WS
  **The project is never written.** A run where
  the agent changed nothing reports no new
  commits, and the operator's own AGENTS.md or
  CLAUDE.md is the only project instruction.
end note

note bottom of MANAGED
  **One block, per boot.** It is written while
  the workspace carries no instructions and
  taken out when it does, so a kept sandbox
  follows the project across restarts.
end note

note bottom of SET
  **Measured, not assumed.** Five managed-file
  variants left AGENTS.md unread on 2.1.312;
  --settings and user settings both read it.
  The operator chose user settings.
end note

note bottom of SIB
  **sbx's sibling CLAUDE.md** counts as a
  CLAUDE.md above the cwd, so Claude Code's
  default skipped every project AGENTS.md.
end note
@enduml
